WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.075
This child was born with a cleft on the left side.

00:00:03.425 --> 00:00:06.283
The pink gum covers a gap in the bone that holds the teeth.

00:00:07.083 --> 00:00:08.982
Without the gum, you can see the gap.

00:00:09.332 --> 00:00:11.615
A bone graft fills this gap with bone.

00:00:12.415 --> 00:00:15.807
2 to 3 years later, bone joins the two parts of the jaw.

00:00:16.157 --> 00:00:20.146
The eye tooth has come down through the new bone, and braces line up the teeth.

00:00:20.946 --> 00:00:22.185
Years later, an implant,

00:00:22.185 --> 00:00:25.490
a bridge or a plate can fill the space where a tooth never grew.

00:00:26.290 --> 00:00:30.087
Or braces move the eye tooth into the gap, and the dentist shapes it.

00:00:30.437 --> 00:00:32.293
Your cleft team will help you choose.
